      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-301668",
      ":question/problem": "A city council wants to estimate the average amount of time residents spend commuting to work each day.\n\nWhich of the following sampling methods is most likely to produce unbiased results?\n\n1. Posting a survey on the city\u2019s website and asking visitors to respond.\n2. Randomly selecting residents from the city census database and contacting them to ask about their commute times.\n3. Asking for responses from people who call into a local radio show about traffic."
