      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-301720",
      ":question/problem": "A financial analyst wants to estimate the average annual return of mutual funds over the past $20$ years.\n\nWhich of the following sampling methods is most likely to produce unbiased results?\n\n1. Selecting funds that are still active today and calculating their past $20$-year returns.\n2. Selecting a random set of funds from the list of all funds that existed at any point in the past $20$ years, including those that have since closed.\n3. Selecting the top-performing funds from the past five years and using their historical returns."
    }
